            "No CSV input file has been supplied; when the CSV milestone is booked, you will need to create or provide a small expenses CSV."
          ],
          "stoppingConditions": [
            "Stop after the tiny total script runs correctly and you explain the loop variable and dictionary lookup; do not start the CSV report until a fresh request."
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "planRef": "plan_2",
      "blueprint": {
        "schemaVersion": 2,
        "strategy": {
          "policy": "ROADMAP",
          "outcome": "Build a JSON expenses report using loops and dictionaries, relying on the shared prerequisite owned by plan_1.",
          "explanation": "This plan does not duplicate the loops/dictionary prerequisite. Its useful next checkpoint is the same tiny total script owned by plan_1; after that is demonstrated, the JSON report can be built later. The JSON report itself remains a strategic milestone and is not booked now.",
          "recommendedEffort": {
            "lowMinutes": 45,
            "likelyMinutes": 75,
            "highMinutes": 120
          },
          "phases": [
            {
              "localId": "json_report",
              "title": "JSON totals report",
              "outcome": "Produce a JSON report of expense totals from a small expenses example.",
              "effort": {
                "lowMinutes": 45,
                "likelyMinutes": 75,
                "highMinutes": 120
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "scope": [
          {
            "scopeRef": "scope_1",
            "disposition": "INCLUDED",
            "contribution": "Uses the shared loops and dictionaries prerequisite owned by plan_1; no separate activity is booked here because the same prerequisite counts once."
          },
          {
            "scopeRef": "scope_2",
            "disposition": "INCLUDED",
            "contribution": "The JSON expenses report is a strategic milestone that becomes useful after the shared loops/dictionary prerequisite is demonstrated; it is not booked now."
          }
        ],
        "activities": [],
        "decisions": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The loops and dictionaries prerequisite is learned through plan_1's committed activity.",
            "JSON report work can wait until that prerequisite is demonstrated."
          ],
          "tradeOffs": [
            "No activity is booked in this plan now; the shared prerequisite is owned by plan_1, and booking it again here would duplicate work.",
            "The JSON report is deferred until the prerequisite is demonstrated and you request the next step."
          ],
          "unresolvedUncertainty": [
            "No expenses data file has been supplied for the JSON report; a small example will need to be created or provided when that milestone is booked.",
            "The exact JSON shape you want is not specified yet."
          ],
          "stoppingConditions": [
            "Stop after the shared loops/dictionary prerequisite is demonstrated; do not start the JSON report until a fresh request."
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "sharedDependencies": [
    {
      "prerequisite": {
        "planRef": "plan_1",
        "activityId": "loops_dict_tiny_total"
      },
      "dependent": {
        "planRef": "plan_2",
        "activityId": "loops_dict_tiny_total"
      },
      "strength": "HARD",
      "reason": "The JSON report depends on the same loops/dictionary prerequisite, which is taught once in plan_1 and must not be duplicated."
    }
  ],
  "tradeOffExplanation": "Only the shared loops/dictionary prerequisite is booked now, as one tiny committed activity in plan_1. The CSV and JSON reports remain strategic and unbooked because you are new to loops and dictionaries; booking them now would exceed the useful next checkpoint. The shared prerequisite is owned by plan_1 and referenced by plan_2, so it counts once. No CSV or JSON example data has been supplied, so those later milestones will need a small example created or provided when requested."
}

