          "outcome": "I say I have mastered circuit methods, but in my self-reported last check I got four of five changed circuits wrong. Do not ignore this contradiction or certify mastery from my claim; choose proportionate education and a meaningful check.",
          "explanation": "The stated outcome is a mastery judgement about independent circuit-method selection, and the only readiness evidence supplied is a self-report that contradicts the mastery claim: four of five changed circuits were wrong. That is not readiness evidence, so nothing can be credited. The proportionate response is a small, honest diagnostic on changed circuits to establish whether the weakness is method choice, execution, or both, and only then a contingent targeted repair. No fixed practice quota is set because the contradiction is the only hard fact; the amount of repair should follow the observed errors. The 60-minute daily ceiling and 30-minute preferred timebox comfortably accommodate one diagnostic; later work is gated on its result.",
          "recommendedEffort": {
            "lowMinutes": 30,
            "likelyMinutes": 60,
            "highMinutes": 120
          },
          "phases": [
            {
              "localId": "diagnose",
              "title": "Diagnose the contradiction",
              "outcome": "A concrete record of which circuit methods you choose on changed circuits, why, and which are solved correctly, so the mastery claim can be judged against actual performance.",
              "effort": {
                "lowMinutes": 30,
                "likelyMinutes": 30,
                "highMinutes": 45
              },
              "readinessCriterion": "Five changed circuits attempted with a stated method choice and reason for each, and each solution checked against the actual circuit behaviour."
