          },
          {
            "localId": "compare_and_explain",
            "outcomeRefs": [
              "diagnose"
            ],
            "scopeRefs": [
              "scope_1"
            ],
            "title": "Compare diagnostic record against actual circuit behaviour",
            "activityType": "Guided review",
            "purpose": "Turn the raw diagnostic into a specific, evidence-based statement of which parts of the mastery claim hold and which do not, so any repair is aimed at real errors rather than the claim.",
            "instructions": "Go through your five items one by one against the actual circuit behaviour. For each item state: the method you chose, whether that method's assumptions and topology genuinely applied, whether your reason was valid, whether your final answer matched the checked result, and if not, the exact step where the error occurred and what the correct step is. Then write a short overall conclusion: on this evidence, is the claim of mastered circuit methods supported, partly supported, or contradicted, and which specific method-selection or execution skills are still missing. Do not treat confidence, time spent, or the number of items as evidence either way; only correct method choice, valid reasons and correct answers count. If the diagnostic was fully correct, say so plainly and do not manufacture errors.",
