              "repair"
            ],
            "scopeRefs": [
              "scope_1"
            ],
            "title": "Targeted repair on new changed circuits",
            "activityType": "Remedial practice",
            "purpose": "Correct the specific errors identified in the comparison on new changed circuits, so the capability is repaired where it actually failed rather than re-taught wholesale.",
            "instructions": "Using only the method-selection errors and execution errors identified in the comparison, work through new changed circuits that exercise exactly those points. For each new circuit, state the method choice and a one-sentence validity reason before solving, then solve and check the answer against the circuit. Cover only the error areas named in the comparison; if the comparison found no errors, this activity is unnecessary and you should stop. If an error area needs a method you were never taught, say so and leave it as an honest gap instead of assuming an advanced method.",
            "completionCriterion": "New changed circuits covering each identified error area are solved with correct method choice, a valid selection reason and a correct checked solution, with no assistance.",
